- Use `opacity` with transitions for animations

### ✍️ Common Array Methods
```js
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

// map
const doubled = numbers.map(num => num * 2);
console.log(doubled);

// filter
const even = numbers.filter(num => num % 2 === 0);
console.log(even);

// find
const found = numbers.find(num => num > 3);
console.log(found);

// reduce
const total = numbers.reduce((sum, num) => sum + num, 0);
console.log(total);
```

### 🔑 Important Methods
- `map()` → transforms array
- `filter()` → filters items
- `find()` → returns first match
- `reduce()` → accumulates values
- `forEach()` → loops through items
- `some()` / `every()` → condition checking

### ⚡ Best Practices
- Prefer array methods over traditional loops in modern JS
- Use immutable patterns when possible
- Chain methods carefully for readability

### ✍️ Basic NgModule Example
```ts
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';

import { AppComponent } from './app.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    AppComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule {}
```

### 🔑 NgModule Properties
- `declarations` → Components, directives, pipes
- `imports` → External modules needed
- `providers` → Services for DI
- `bootstrap` → Starting/root component
- `exports` → Shares components with other modules

